              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Visual Patterns**\n\nI'm currently focused on dissecting the training data. The examples present visual grids with colored borders and colored points inside. My objective now is to identify the relationship between the border colors and the position of the colored points within the grid, particularly when those points are the color 1.\n\n\n**Interpreting Proximity Rules**\n\nI think I've cracked a proximity-based logic. It looks like the column index of each point is assessed for proximity to the edges. Based on how close a point's column index is to column 0 or column 9, a 4 or an 8 is output. It appears the output is generated adjacent to that point on the grid. I'm going to solidify this with the second example.\n\n\n**Refining Border Logic**\n\nI've made a breakthrough with the border logic, I think. It looks like the output depends on the proximity to the closer border, and it seems the pixel is moved to the adjacent cell to that border. The distance from the point to each border matters. Now I'm checking if the distance to the closer border determines which value is generated for the new cell, to solidify my model.\n\n\n",
